<Input>
<Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" spaceabove="10">The inductive hypothesis is that <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> is divisible by 7 for a positive integer <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEia0YnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEia0YnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy9GM1Enbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation>.  We need to show that <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> is divisible by 7.  To do this, we'll use the following fact: if <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> and <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> then <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>.  (The reader should verify this statement, which is equivalent to Theorem 1, part (i), of Section 4.1.)  </Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
